        <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
        <h1 class="h1">Your information stays yours.</h1>
        <p class="lede" style="margin-top:20px;">We build apps that need as little of your information as possible. This page explains, in plain English, what each one uses and why.</p>
        <p class="muted">Last updated 16 November 2026</p>

        <h2 id="enroute">Enroute</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>No account is needed</strong> to track trains, and Enroute never asks for your email address.</li>
          <li><strong>Your journeys</strong> are stored on your iPhone and, if you use iCloud, synced through your own private iCloud account. Metro Studio does not hold a database of anyone's travel.</li>
          <li><strong>Location</strong> is used once, only when you ask for departures near you, to find your nearest station. It isn't stored or shared.</li>
          <li><strong>Sign in with Apple</strong> is optional and only used for Friends. Sign-in details are kept in your device's Keychain, and you can revoke access at any time.</li>
          <li><strong>Friends</strong> see the train you choose to share (its route, estimated position and status), never your own location. Sharing is read-only and you can remove anyone's access at any moment.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="mywashingline">MyWashingLine</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>No account</strong> and no sign-up.</li>
          <li><strong>Location</strong> is requested only while you're using the app, to show the forecast where you are. You can search for a place instead.</li>
          <li><strong>Weather</strong> comes from MET Norway. To fetch a forecast, the app sends them the place's coordinates, rounded to four decimal places. No personal details are sent.</li>
          <li><strong>Saved places</strong> are stored on your device only. There is no cloud sync.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="studio">This website</h2>
        <p>This site doesn't use cookies, advertising or tracking. If you email us, we'll use your message only to reply to you.</p>

        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@metro-studio.co.uk">hello@metro-studio.co.uk</a> and we'll get back to you.</p>
